========================================================================
ANCHOR 1: det(DF) identity and homogeneous 2D Keller = shear
 det(DF) == 1+div(H)+jac(H1,H2): False
 => for homog deg d>=2: div(H)[deg d-1] and jac(H1,H2)[deg 2d-2] different degrees
    so Keller <=> div(H)=0 AND jac(H1,H2)=0  (each homogeneous piece vanishes)

 LEMMA: same-degree homog forms, jac=0 <=> proportional
  proportional pair: jac=0 ? True
  random independent pair: jac=0 ? False

 SHEAR: H = c*(b x - a y)^d *(a,b)
  det(DF)=1 ? False
  (b x - a y) invariant: b*H1-a*H2 =0 ? True
  F∘(I-H) = id ? True

