ANCHOR 1 (fixed): det(DF)=jac(F1,F2) directly
 identity det(DF)==1+div(H)+jac(H1,H2): True
 shear det(DF)=1 ? True

========================================================================
ANCHOR 2: leading-form power structure + the descent dichotomy
 Claim: jac(f_n,g_m)=0  <=>  f_n=α h^p, g_m=β h^q  (common form h);
        equivalently f_n^(m/g) = const * g_m^(n/g),  g=gcd(n,m).
  single-root h=l^k      n=4,m=6,gcd=2: jac(f_n,g_m)=0? True  f_n^(m/g)=const*g_m^(n/g)? False
  multi-root h           n=4,m=6,gcd=2: jac(f_n,g_m)=0? True  f_n^(m/g)=const*g_m^(n/g)? True
  coprime deg, h linear  n=3,m=5,gcd=1: jac(f_n,g_m)=0? True  f_n^(m/g)=const*g_m^(n/g)? True

 DESCENT MOVES (reduce degree by killing the common leading form):
  * n=m  => f_n,g_m proportional => g' = g - (β/α) f  drops deg g. ALWAYS reduces.
  * n!=m, q|p (i.e. m|n)  => f' = f - (α/β^(p/q)) g^(p/q) drops deg f. Reduces.
  * n!<m and m!|n  (neither divides) => leading form cannot be killed by a power.
    THIS is the stuck stratum (Abhyankar-Moh). Verify a reduce vs a stuck case:
    m|n reduce: deg f=4 -> deg(f - g^2)=3 (dropped: True)

========================================================================
ANCHOR 3: places at infinity = DISTINCT roots of the leading form h
  Keller pair f_n=a h^p, g_m=b h^q share the SAME places (roots of h).
  single-root h=(x-cy)^3 : distinct roots = 1  repeated?  True  => 1 place at infinity
  multi-root (3 distinct): distinct roots = 3  repeated?  False  => 3 places at infinity

  CLASSICAL CONSEQUENCE (Abhyankar-Moh): ONE place at infinity => the affine
  curve embeds as a coordinate line => the pencil is tame. So:
    single-root leading form h  =>  1 place at infinity  =>  TAME (no counterexample)
    JC(2) counterexamples REQUIRE a multi-root (>=2 distinct roots) leading form h.
